---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import GitHubIcon from '../components/icons/GitHubIcon.astro';
import LinkedInIcon from '../components/icons/LinkedInIcon.astro';
import ThemeToggle from '../components/ThemeToggle.astro';

const currentYear = new Date().getFullYear();
const lastUpdated = 'June 30, 2026';
const GITHUB_URL = 'https://github.com/farengeyt451/seenit-episode-tracker';
const LINKEDIN_URL = 'https://www.linkedin.com/in/alexander-kislov/';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy - Seenit! Episode Tracker"
  description="Privacy Policy for the Seenit! - Episode Tracker browser extension."
>
  <div class="page">
    <header class="header">
      <a href="/" class="logo" aria-label="Seenit! home">
        <img src="/icon-128.png" alt="Seenit! logo" class="logo__mark" width="32" height="32" />
        <span class="logo__text">Seenit!</span>
      </a>
      <div class="header__actions">
        <a
          href={GITHUB_URL}
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="header__link"
          aria-label="GitHub"
        >
          <GitHubIcon />
        </a>
        <a
          href={LINKEDIN_URL}
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="header__link"
          aria-label="LinkedIn"
        >
          <LinkedInIcon />
        </a>
        <ThemeToggle />
      </div>
    </header>

    <main class="main">
      <article class="legal">
        <h1 class="legal__title">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="legal__meta">Seenit! - Episode Tracker · Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

        <p>
          This Privacy Policy explains how the <strong>Seenit! - Episode Tracker</strong> browser
          extension handles your information. Seenit! is designed to be private by default: your data
          stays on your device and, optionally, in your own Google Drive. There are no servers that
          collect or store your personal data.
        </p>

        <h2>1. Data Stored</h2>
        <p>
          Seenit! stores the data needed to track your shows, including the series you add, your
          episode and season watch progress, favorites, and your app settings (such as theme).
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Local storage:</strong> By default, all of this data is stored locally in your browser
            using the Chrome Storage API. It never leaves your device unless Cloud Sync is enabled.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Optional Google Drive sync:</strong> If you choose to connect Google Drive, your tracking
            data is saved to the private, hidden <code>application data</code> folder of <em>your own</em> Google
            Drive account so it can sync across your devices.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>2. Google User Data &amp; OAuth Scopes</h2>
        <p>When you enable Cloud Sync, Seenit! requests a single, minimal Google OAuth scope:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <code>https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive.appdata</code> -access to a dedicated, hidden
            application-data folder in your Google Drive.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          This scope <strong>cannot</strong> access, read, or modify any of your other Google Drive files,
          photos, or documents. It is limited exclusively to the hidden folder that Seenit! creates for
          its own sync data. No other scope is requested.
        </p>
        <p>
          Seenit!'s use of information received from Google APIs adheres to the
          <a
            href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer">Google API Services User Data Policy</a
          >, including the Limited Use requirements.
        </p>

        <h2>3. How Your Data Is Used</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>To display and track the TV shows and episodes you are watching.</li>
          <li>To sync your tracking data across your own devices (only if Cloud Sync is enabled).</li>
          <li>To save your preferences and settings.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Your data is <strong>not</strong> used for advertising, profiling, or any purpose other than
          providing the core functionality of the extension.
        </p>

        <h2>4. Data Sharing</h2>
        <p>
          Your data is <strong>never</strong> sold, rented, traded, or transferred to any third party.
          Seenit! has no backend servers of its own. The only external services involved are:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Google Drive API</strong> -only when you opt in to Cloud Sync, and only to store data
            in your own Drive's hidden app folder.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>TheTVDB API</strong> -to fetch publicly available series and episode metadata
            (e.g. show titles, ratings, genres, air dates). No personal data is sent to this service.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>5. Data Retention &amp; Deletion</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Local data:</strong> Removed when you delete the data within the extension, clear your
            browser data, or uninstall Seenit!.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Google Drive data:</strong> You can disconnect Google Drive at any time from the extension's
            Settings, which revokes access. You may also delete the stored app data directly from your
            Google Drive account.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>6. Security</h2>
        <p>
          Your data is stored within your browser and your own Google Drive account, protected by your
          Google account's security. Communication with Google APIs uses encrypted HTTPS connections.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Children's Privacy</h2>
        <p>
          Seenit! is not directed to children under the age of 13 and does not knowingly collect personal
          information from children.
        </p>

        <h2>8. Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p>
          This Privacy Policy may be updated from time to time. Changes will be reflected on this page with
          an updated "Last updated" date.
        </p>

        <h2>9. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about this Privacy Policy can be sent to:
          <a href="mailto:seenitapp@outlook.com">seenitapp@outlook.com</a>
        </p>

        <p class="legal__back"><a href="/">← Back to home</a></p>
      </article>
    </main>

    <footer class="footer">
      <div class="footer__links">
        <a href="/privacy" class="footer__link">Privacy Policy</a>
        <span class="footer__sep">·</span>
        <a href={GITHUB_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="footer__link">GitHub</a>
        <span class="footer__sep">·</span>
        <a
          href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/alexander-kislov/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="footer__link">LinkedIn</a
        >
      </div>
      <p class="footer__copyright">© Seenit! - {currentYear}</p>
    </footer>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .logo {
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .logo__mark {
    width: 32px;
    height: 32px;
    border-radius: 8px;
    display: block;
  }

  .legal {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 3.5rem 1.5rem 5rem;
  }

  .legal__title {
    font-family: 'Poppins', system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-size: 2.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--gradient-blue), var(--gradient-purple), var(--gradient-pink));
    -webkit-background-clip: text;
    -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent;
    background-clip: text;
  }

  .legal__meta {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .legal :global(h2) {
    font-family: 'Poppins', system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    margin: 2.5rem 0 0.75rem;
    padding-bottom: 0.4rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color);
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  .legal :global(p) {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .legal :global(ul) {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .legal :global(li) {
    margin: 0.4rem 0;
  }

  .legal :global(strong) {
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  .legal :global(a) {
    color: var(--accent-blue);
  }

  .legal :global(code) {
    background: var(--bg-surface);
    padding: 0.1em 0.4em;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 0.9em;
    word-break: break-all;
  }

  .legal__back {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
  }

  .footer__links {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .footer__link {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .footer__link:hover {
    color: var(--accent-blue);
  }

  .footer__sep {
    color: var(--text-tertiary);
  }

  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    .legal__title {
      font-size: 2rem;
    }
  }
</style>
